# Python Code Execution Prevention

## Security Rules

- NEVER execute Python code or run Python scripts
- NEVER run `python`, `python3`, or any Python interpreter commands
- NEVER execute the main.py script or any other Python files
- NEVER run pip, uv, or any package manager commands that could execute code
- NEVER run any commands that could potentially execute Python code

## Allowed Actions

- Read and analyze Python code files
- Edit Python code files
- Search through the codebase
- View file contents and directory structures
- Make code suggestions and improvements
- Test syntax and logic without execution

## Security Rationale

This project contains code that could potentially make network requests and access external resources. Code execution is strictly prohibited to prevent any unintended side effects or security risks.

## When Asked to Test or Run Code

If asked to test or run Python code:

1. Explain that code execution is not allowed per project rules
2. Offer to review the code for syntax errors or logical issues
3. Suggest manual testing by the user if needed
4. Provide code analysis and suggestions instead
